#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:49
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:52
msgid ""
"This RFC builds on a large collection of prior art collated in the [`build-"
"std-context`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3873-build-std-context."
"html#proposal) RFC. It does not directly address the main [rfcs#3873-"
"motivation](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3873-build-std-context."
"html#motivation) it identifies but supports later proposals."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:56
msgid ""
"The main motivation for this proposal is to support future extensions to "
"build-std which allow public/private standard library dependencies or "
"enabling features of the standard library. Allowing the standard library to "
"behave similarly to other dependencies also reduces user friction and can "
"improve build times."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:62
msgid "Proposal"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:65
msgid ""
"Users can now optionally declare explicit dependencies on the standard "
"library in their `Cargo.toml` files ([?](#why-explicitly-declare-"
"dependencies-on-the-standard-library-in-cargotoml)):"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:68
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { builtin = true }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:78
msgid ""
"`builtin` is a new source of dependency, like registry dependencies (with "
"the `version` key and optionally the `registry` key), `path` dependencies or "
"`git` dependencies. `builtin` can only be set to `true` and cannot be "
"combined with any other dependency source for a given dependency ([?](#why-"
"disallow-builtin-dependencies-to-be-combined-with-other-sources))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:84
msgid ""
"`builtin` can only be used with crates named `core`, `alloc` or `std` ([?]"
"(#why-disallow-builtin-dependencies-on-other-crates)) on stable. This set "
"could be expanded with new crates in future."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:88
msgid ""
"Use with any other crate name is gated on a perma-unstable `cargo-feature` "
"([?](#why-unstably-allow-all-names-for-builtin-crates)). If a builtin "
"dependency on a unstable crate name exists but is not used due to cfgs, then "
"Cargo will still require the Cargo feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:93
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:113
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:203
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:439
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:598
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:652
msgid "\\[!NOTE\\]"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:95
msgid ""
"Explicit dependencies are passed to rustc without the `noprelude` modifier "
"([?](#why-not-use-noprelude-for-explicit-builtin-dependencies)) (`noprelude` "
"refers to the compiler's notion of the \"extern prelude\", not the prelude "
"in the the user-facing sense of `std::prelude::*`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:100
msgid ""
"When adding an explicit dependency, users may need to adjust their code "
"(removing extraneous `extern crate` statements or root-relative paths, like "
"`::std` - this will likely only be the case on the 2015 edition)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:104
msgid ""
"Crates without an explicit dependency on the standard library now have a "
"implicit dependency ([?](#why-not-require-builtin-dependencies-instead-of-"
"supporting-implicit-ones)) on that target's default set of standard library "
"crates (see [build-std-always](https://github.com/davidtwco/rfcs/blob/build-"
"std-part-two-always/text/3874-build-std-always.md#standard-library-crate-"
"stability)). Any explicit standard library dependency present in any "
"dependency table applicable to the current target will disable the implicit "
"dependencies (e.g. an explicit `builtin` or `path` dependency from `std` "
"will disable the implicit dependencies)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:115
msgid ""
"Implicit dependencies are passed to rustc with the `noprelude` modifier to "
"ensure backwards compatibility as in [`build-std=always`](https://github.com/"
"davidtwco/rfcs/blob/build-std-part-two-always/text/3874-build-std-always."
"md#why-use-noprelude-with---extern)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:119
msgid ""
"When a `std` dependency is present an additional implicit dependency on the "
"`test` crate is added for crates that are being tested with the default test "
"harness. The `test` crate's name, but not its interface, will be stabilised "
"so Cargo can refer to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:124
msgid ""
"crates.io will accept crates published which have `builtin` dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:126
msgid ""
"Standard library dependencies can be marked as `optional` and be enabled "
"conditionally by a feature in the crate:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:129
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { builtin = true, optional = true }\n"
"core = { builtin = true }\n"
"\n"
"[features]\n"
"default = [\"std\"]\n"
"std = [\"dep:std\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:144
msgid ""
"If there is an optional dependency on the standard library then Cargo will "
"validate that there is at least one non-optional dependency on the standard "
"library (e.g. an optional `std` and non-optional `core` or `alloc`, or an "
"optional `alloc` and non-optional `core`). `core` cannot be optional. For "
"example, the following example will error as it could result in a build "
"without `core` (if the `std` feature were disabled):"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:151
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { builtin = true, optional = true }\n"
"# error: must have a non-optional dependency on core\n"
"\n"
"[features]\n"
"default = [\"std\"]\n"
"std = [\"dep:std\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:166
msgid ""
"However, in this example, a build for the `x86-64-pc-windows-gnu` target "
"would have an explicit dependency on `alloc` (and indirectly on `core`), "
"while a build for any other target would have implicit dependencies on "
"`std`, `alloc` and `core`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:171
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"# implicit deps on `core`, `alloc` and `std` unless target='x86_64-pc-"
"windows-gnu'\n"
"\n"
"[target.x86_64-pc-windows-gnu.dependencies]\n"
"alloc.builtin = true\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:184
msgid ""
"Dependencies with `builtin = true` cannot be renamed with the `package` key "
"([?](#why-disallow-renaming-standard-library-dependencies)). It is not "
"possible to perform source replacement on the `builtin` source using the "
"`[source]` Cargo config table ([?](#why-disallow-source-replacement-on-"
"builtin-packages)), and nor is it possible to override `builtin` "
"dependencies with the `[replace]` sections or `paths` overrides ([?](#why-"
"not-permit-overriding-dependencies-with-replace-or-paths)), though [patching]"
"(#patches) is permitted under a perma-unstable feature flag ([?](#why-"
"unstably-permit-patching-of-the-standard-library-dependencies))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:192
msgid ""
"Dependencies with `builtin = true` can be specified as platform-specific "
"dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:200
msgid ""
"Implicit and explicit standard library dependencies are added to `Cargo."
"lock` files ([?](#why-add-standard-library-dependencies-to-cargolock))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:205
msgid ""
"A new version of the `Cargo.lock` file will be introduced to add support for "
"packages with a `builtin` source:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:208
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[[package]]\n"
"name = \"std\"\n"
"version = \"0.0.0\"\n"
"source = \"builtin\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:215
msgid ""
"The package version of `std`, `alloc` and `core` will be fixed at `0.0.0`. "
"The optional lockfile fields `dependencies` and `checksum` will not be "
"present for `builtin` dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:219
msgid ""
"A perma-unstable Cargo feature for disabling all standard library "
"dependencies will be added to allow the `core` crate to be defined."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:222
msgid ""
"When a crate has no builtin dependency on `std` (or an optional builtin "
"dependency on `std`), then Cargo will pass `-Zcrate-attr=no_std` to rustc "
"(or some equivalent; [?](#why-pass--zcrate-attrno_std-to-rustc))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:226
msgid ""
"Builtin dependencies defined in `workspace.dependencies` are inherited by "
"members of the workspace in the same way as any other dependency and then "
"the same behaviour and constraints apply."
msgstr ""

