#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:257
msgid "Non-`builtin` standard library dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:260
msgid ""
"Cargo already supports `path` and `git` dependencies for crates named "
"`core`, `alloc` and `std` which continue to be supported and work:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:263
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { path = \"../my_std\" } # already supported by Cargo\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:273
msgid ""
"A `core`/`alloc`/`std` dependency with a `path`/`git` source can be combined "
"with `builtin` dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:276
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { path = \"../my_std\" }\n"
"core = { builtin = true }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:287
msgid ""
"Crates with these dependency sources will remain unable to be published to "
"crates.io."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:290
msgid ""
"Building on both of the above, a `core`/`alloc`/`std` dependency can have "
"`path`/`git` source at the same time as a `builtin` source. This allows the "
"crate to remain publishable while the `path`/`git` source is only used "
"locally:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:294
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { builtin = true, path = \"../my_std\" } # published as `builtin` dep, "
"`path` used locally\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:304
msgid ""
"This mirrors the existing behaviour for `path`/`git` sources when combined "
"with registry sources."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:307
msgid "Patches"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:310
msgid ""
"Under a perma-unstable feature it is permitted to patch standard library "
"dependencies with `path` and `git` sources (or any other source) ([?](#why-"
"unstably-permit-patching-of-the-standard-library-dependencies)):"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:314
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { builtin = true }\n"
"\n"
"[patch.builtin] # permitted on nightly\n"
"std = { path = \"../libstd\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:327
msgid ""
"As with dependencies, crates with `path`/`git` patches for `core`, `alloc` "
"or `std` are not accepted by crates.io."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:332
msgid ""
"[_Why unstably permit patching of standard library dependencies?_](#why-"
"unstably-permit-patching-of-the-standard-library-dependencies)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:336
msgid ""
"[_What syntax is used to patch dependencies on the standard library in "
"`Cargo.toml`?_](#what-syntax-is-used-to-patch-dependencies-on-the-standard-"
"library-in-cargotoml)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:338
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:341
msgid ""
"On a stable toolchain, it is not permitted to enable or disable features of "
"explicit standard library dependencies ([?](#why-limit-enabling-standard-"
"library-features-to-an-unstable-feature)), as in the below example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:345
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { builtin = true, features = [ \"foo\" ] } # not permitted\n"
"# ..or..\n"
"std = { builtin = true, default-features = false } # not permitted\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:359
msgid ""
"[_Why limit enabling standard library features to an unstable feature?_]"
"(#why-limit-enabling-standard-library-features-to-an-unstable-feature)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:363
msgid ""
"[_Allow enabling/disabling features with build-std_](#allow-"
"enablingdisabling-features-with-build-std)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:365
msgid "Public and private dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:368
msgid ""
"Implicit dependencies on the standard library default to being public "
"dependencies ([?](#why-default-to-public-for-implicit-standard-library-"
"dependencies))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:371
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:380
msgid "..is equivalent to the following explicit dependency on `std`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:382
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
