#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:506
msgid ""
"Any Cargo command which accepts a package spec with `-p` will now "
"additionally recognise `core`, `alloc` and `std` and none of their "
"dependencies. Many of Cargo's subcommands will need modification to support "
"build-std:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:510
msgid ""
"[`cargo add`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-add.html)'s "
"heuristics will include adding `std`, `alloc` or `core` as builtin "
"dependencies if these crate names are provided. `cargo add` will "
"additionally have a `--builtin` flag to allow for adding crates with a "
"`builtin` source explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:515
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"hello_world\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"std = { builtin = true } # <-- this would be added\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:525
msgid ""
"If attempting to add a crate name outside of `core`, `alloc` or `std` this "
"will fail unless the required `cargo-feature` is added to allow other "
