#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:760
msgid "Rationale and alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:763
msgid ""
"This section aims to justify all of the decisions made in the proposed "
"design from [_Proposal_](#proposal) and discuss why alternatives were not "
"chosen."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:766
msgid ""
"Why explicitly declare dependencies on the standard library in `Cargo.toml`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:769
msgid ""
"If there are no explicit dependencies on standard library crates, Cargo "
"would need to be able to determine which standard library crates to build "
"when this is required:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:773
msgid ""
"Cargo could unconditionally build `std`, `alloc` and `core`. Not only would "
"this be unnecessary and wasteful for `no_std` crates in the embedded "
"ecosystem, but sometimes a target may not support building `std` at all and "
"this would cause the build to fail."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:778
msgid ""
"rustc could support a `--print` value that would print whether the crate "
"declares itself as `#![no_std]` crate, and based on this, Cargo could build "
"`std` or only `core`. This would require asking rustc to parse crates' "
"sources while resolving dependencies, slowing build times. Alternatively, "
"Cargo can already read Rust source to detect frontmatter (for `cargo "
"script`) so it could additionally look for `#![no_std]` itself. Regardless "
"of how it determines a crate is no-std, Cargo would also need to know "
"whether to build `alloc` too, which checking for `#![no_std]` does not help "
"with. Cargo could go further and ask rustc whether a crate (or its "
"dependencies) used `alloc`, but this seems needlessly complicated."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:789
msgid ""
"Cargo could allow the user to specify which crates are required to be built, "
"such as with the existing options to the `-Zbuild-std=` flag. [`build-"
"std=always`](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3874-build-std-always."
"html#proposal) proposes a `build-std.crates` flag to enable explicit "
"dependencies to be a separate part of this RFC."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:794
msgid ""
"Furthermore, supporting explicit dependencies on standard library crates "
"enables use of other Cargo features that apply to dependencies in a natural "
"and intuitive way. If there were not explicit standard library dependencies "
"and enabling features on the `std` crate was desirable, then a mechanism "
"other than the standard syntax for this would be necessary, such as a flag "
"(e.g. `-Zbuild-std-features`) or option in Cargo's configuration. This also "
"applies to optional dependencies, public/private features, etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:802
msgid ""
"Users already use Cargo features to toggle `#![no_std]` in crates which "
"support building without the standard library. When dependencies on the "
"standard library are exposed in `Cargo.toml` then they can be made optional "
"and enabled by the existing Cargo features that crates already have."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:807
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:832
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:849
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:867
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:884
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:901
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:917
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:931
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:939
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:951
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:970
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1105
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1114
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1245
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1256
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1267
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1282
msgid "↩ [_Proposal_](#proposal)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:809
msgid "Why disallow builtin dependencies to be combined with other sources?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:812
msgid ""
"If using `path`/`git` sources with `builtin` dependencies worked in the same "
"way as using `path`/`git` sources with `version` sources, then: crates with "
"`path`/`git` standard library dependencies could be pushed to crates.io."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:816
msgid ""
"This is not desirable as it is unclear that supporting `path`/`git` sources "
"which shadow standard library crates was a deliberate choice and so enabling "
"that pattern to be used more widely when not necessary is needlessly "
"permissive."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:820
msgid ""
"In addition, when combined with a `git`/`path` source, the `version` "
"constraint also applies to package from the `git`/`path` source. If "
"`version` were used alongside `builtin`, then this behaviour would be a poor "
"fit as.."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:824
msgid ""
"..the `std`, `alloc` and `core` crates all currently have a version of "
"`0.0.0`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:826
msgid ""
"..choosing different version requirements for different `builtin` crates is "
"confusing when a single version of these crates is provided by the toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:829
msgid ""
"Hypothetically, choosing a different version for `builtin` crates could be a "
"way of supporting per-target/per-profile MSRVs, but this has limited utility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:834
msgid "Why disallow builtin dependencies on other crates?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:837
msgid ""
"`builtin` dependencies could be accepted on two other crates - dependencies "
"of the standard library, like `compiler_builtins`, or other crates in the "
"sysroot added manually by users, however:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:841
msgid ""
"The standard library's dependencies are not part of the stable interface of "
"the standard library and it is not desirable that users can observe their "
"existence or depend on them directly"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:845
msgid ""
"Other crates in the sysroot added by users are not something that can "
"reasonably be supported by build-std and these crates should become regular "
"dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:851
msgid "Why unstably allow all names for `builtin` crates?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:854
msgid ""
"For any crate shipped with the standard library in the sysroot, the user can "
"already write an `extern crate` declaration to use it. Most are marked "
"unstable either explicitly or implicitly with the use of `-Zforce-unstable-"
"if-unmarked` so this does not allow items from these crates to be used on "
"stable."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:859
msgid ""
"For example, some users write benchmarks using `libtest` and have written "
"`extern crate test` without the `#[cfg(test)]` attribute to load the crate. "
"There may be other niche uses of unstable sysroot crates that this enables "
"to continue on nightly toolchains."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:864
msgid ""
"An allowlist of `builtin` crate names isn't used here to avoid Cargo needing "
"to hardcode the names of many crates in the sysroot which are inherently "
"unstable."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:869
msgid "Why not use `noprelude` for explicit `builtin` dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:872
msgid ""
"Explicit builtin dependencies without the `noprelude` modifier behave more "
"consistently with other dependencies specified in the Cargo manifest."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:875
msgid ""
"This is a trade-off, trading consistency of user experience with special-"
"casing in Cargo. Cargo would have to handle implicit vs explicit "
"dependencies differently. An explicit dependency on the standard library "
"will behave similarly to other dependencies in their manifest, but the "
"behaviour will be subtly different than with implicit builtin dependencies "
"(where `extern crate` is required)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:882
msgid ""
"See [the rustc documentation for more details on `noprelude`](https://doc."
"rust-lang.org/nightly/unstable-book/compiler-flags/extern-options.html#--"
"extern-options)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:888
msgid ""
"Why not require builtin dependencies instead of supporting implicit ones?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:891
msgid ""
"Requiring explicit `builtin` dependencies over an edition would increase the "
"boilerplate required for users of Cargo and make the minimal `Cargo.toml` "
"file larger."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:895
msgid ""
"Supporting implicit dependencies allows the majority of the Rust ecosystem "
"from having to make any changes - `no_std` crates (or crates with a `std` "
"feature) will still benefit from adding explicit dependencies as allow them "
"to be easily used with `no_std` targets but users can still work around any "
"legacy crates in the graph with [`build-std.crates`](https://rust-lang."
"github.io/rfcs/3874-build-std-always.html#proposal)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:903
msgid "Why disallow renaming standard library dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:906
msgid ""
"Cargo allows [renaming dependencies](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/"
"reference/specifying-dependencies.html#renaming-dependencies-in-cargotoml) "
"with the `package` key, which allows user code to refer to dependencies by "
"names which do not match their `package` name in their respective `Cargo."
"toml` files."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:910
msgid ""
"However, rustc expects the standard library crates to be present with their "
"existing names - for example, `core` is always added to the [extern prelude]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/names/preludes.html#extern-prelude)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:914
msgid ""
"Alternatively, a mechanism could be added to rustc so that it could be "
"informed of the user's names for `builtin` crates."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:922
msgid "Why disallow source replacement on `builtin` packages?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:925
msgid ""
"Modifying the source code of the standard library in the `rust-src` "
"component is not supported. Source replacement of the `builtin` source could "
"be a way to support this in future but this is out-of-scope for this "
"proposal."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:929
msgid ""
"See [_Allow `builtin` source replacement_](#allow-builtin-source-"
"replacement)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:933
msgid "Why not permit overriding dependencies with `replace` or `paths`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:936
msgid ""
"Similarly to [source replacement](#why-disallow-source-replacement-on-"
"builtin-packages), easing modification of the standard library sources is "
"out-of-scope for this proposal."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:941
msgid "Why add standard library dependencies to `Cargo.lock`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:944
msgid ""
"`Cargo.lock` is a direct serialisation of a resolve and that must be a two-"
"way non-lossy process in order to make the `Cargo.lock` useful without doing "
"further resolution to fill in missing `builtin` packages."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:948
msgid ""
"Cargo will nevertheless need to support lockfiles without builtin "
"dependencies as Cargo does not force new lockfile versions."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:953
msgid "Why pass `-Zcrate-attr=no_std` to rustc?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:956
msgid ""
"The introduction of explicit dependencies means that there are now two ways "
"to indicate whether a crate depends on the standard library - builtin "
"dependencies in the Cargo manifest and the `#![no_std]` attribute. This "
"isn't ideal."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:960
msgid ""
"By passing `-Zcrate-attr=no_std` to rustc (or some equivalent), users no "
"longer need to specify the attribute explicitly in their source code. The "
"attribute can still be explicitly specified this way, which is useful when "
"rustc is used without a build system like Cargo. Other build systems can "
"similarly pass `-Zcrate-attr=no_std` if emulating how build-std works in "
"Cargo."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:966
msgid ""
"Removing or replacing `#![no_std]` as a mechanism is left as a follow-up to "
"avoid introducing a language change in this RFC - see [_Replace `#![no_std]` "
"as the source-of-truth for whether a crate depends on `std`_](#replace-"
"no_std-as-the-source-of-truth-for-whether-a-crate-depends-on-std)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:972
msgid "Why unstably permit patching of the standard library dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:975
msgid ""
"Being able to patch `builtin = true` dependencies and replace their source "
"with a `path` dependency is required to be able to replace "
"`rustc_dep_of_std`. As crates which use these sources cannot be published to "
"crates.io, this would not enable a usable general-purpose mechanism for "
"crates to modify the standard library sources. This capability is restricted "
"to nightly toolchains as that is all that is required for it to be used in "
"replacing `rustc_dep_of_std`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:982
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1123
msgid "↩ [_Patches_](#patches)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:984
msgid "Why limit enabling standard library features to an unstable feature?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:987
msgid ""
"If it were possible to enable features of the standard library crates on "
"stable then all of the standard library's current features would immediately "
"be held to the same stability guarantees as the rest of the standard "
"library, which is not desirable. See [_Allow enabling/disabling features "
"with build-std_](#allow-enablingdisabling-features-with-build-std)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:993
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1302
msgid "↩ [_Features_](#features)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:995
msgid "Why default to public for implicit standard library dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:998
msgid ""
"There are crates building on stable which re-export from the standard "
"library. If implicit standard library dependencies were not public then "
"these crates would start to trigger the `exported_private_dependencies` lint "
"when upgrading to a version of Cargo with a implicit standard library "
"dependency."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1003
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1014
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1133
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1142
msgid "↩ [_Public and private dependencies_](#public-and-private-dependencies)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1005
msgid "Why default to private for explicit standard library dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1008
msgid ""
"All other explicitly written dependencies in the Cargo manifest are private-"
"by-default. This RFC tries to make builtin dependencies as consistent with "
"other dependencies in the manifest as possible (e.g. in [_Why not use "
"`noprelude` for explicit `builtin` dependencies?_](#why-not-use-noprelude-"
"for-explicit-builtin-dependencies))."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1016
msgid "Why include standard library crates in Cargo's index format?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1019
msgid ""
"When Cargo builds the unit graph - roughly speaking, think of this as the "
"compiler invocations it will eventually make - it queries the dependency "
"resolver as to which dependencies a given crate has. The dependency resolver "
"only looks at the source of a dependency, in many cases a registry source (i."
"e. a dependency from crates.io). In practice, this is the entry in the Cargo "
"index for that dependency. As this is the information that is directly "
"available, that a crate depends on the standard library should be reflected "
"in the index entry."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1027
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the Cargo manifests of dependencies would need to be parsed "
"in order to determine whether they have standard library dependencies as the "
"index entry would be insufficient."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1031
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1074
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1090
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1165
msgid "↩ [_Registries_](#registries)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1033
msgid "Why add a new key to Cargo's registry index JSON schema?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1036
msgid ""
"Cargo's [registry index schema](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/"
"registry-index.html#json-schema) is versioned and making a behaviour-of-"
"Cargo-modifying change to the existing `deps` keys would be a breaking "
"change. Each package is published under one particular version of the "
"schema, meaning that older versions of Cargo cannot use newer versions of "
"packages which are defined using a schema it does not have knowledge of."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1042
msgid ""
"Cargo ignores packages published under an unsupported schema version, so "
"older versions of Cargo cannot use newer versions of packages relying on "
"these features (though this would be true because of an incompatible Cargo "
"manifest anyway). New schema versions are disruptive to users on older "
"toolchains, as the resolver will act as if a package does not exist. Recent "
"Cargo versions have improved error reporting for this circumstance."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1049
msgid ""
"Some new fields, including `rust-version`, were added to all versions of the "
"schema. Cargo ignores fields it does not have knowledge of, so older "
"versions of Cargo will simply not use `rust-version` and its presence does "
"not change their behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1054
msgid ""
"Existing versions of Cargo already function correctly without knowledge of "
"crate's standard library dependencies. A new top-level key will be ignored "
"by older versions of Cargo, while newer versions will understand it. This is "
"a different approach to that taken when artifact dependencies were added to "
"the schema, as those do not have a suitable representation in older versions "
"of Cargo."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1061
msgid ""
"The obvious alternative to a `builtin_deps` key is to modify `deps` entries "
"with a new `builtin: bool` field and to increment the version of the schema. "
"However, these entries would not be understood by older versions of Cargo "
"which would look in the registry to find these packages and fail to do so."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1066
msgid ""
"That approach could be made to work if dummy packages for `core`/`alloc`/"
"`std` were added to registries. Older versions of Cargo would pass these to "
"rustc via `--extern` and shadow the real standard library dependencies in "
"the sysroot, so these packages would need to contain `extern crate std; pub "
"use std::*;` (and similar for `alloc`/`core`) to try and load the pre-built "
"libraries from the sysroot (this is the same approach as packages like "
"[embed-rs](https://github.com/embed-rs/stm32f7-discovery/blob/"
"e2bf713263791c028c2a897f2eb1830d7f09eceb/core/src/lib.rs#L7) take today, "
"using `path` dependencies for the standard library to shadow it)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1079
msgid "Why can `builtin_deps` shadow other packages in the registry?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1082
msgid ""
"While `crates.io` forbids certain crate names including `std`, `alloc` and "
"`core`, third party registries may allow them without a warning. The schema "
"needs a way to refer to packages with the same name either in the registry "
"or builtin, which `builtin_deps` allows."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1087
msgid ""
"`builtin_deps` names are not allowed to shadow names of packages in `deps` "
"as these would conflict when passed to rustc via `--extern`."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1092
msgid "Unresolved questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1095
msgid ""
"The following small details are likely to be bikeshed prior to this part of "
"the RFC's acceptance or stabilisation and aren't pertinent to the overall "
"design:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1098
msgid ""
"What syntax is used to identify dependencies on the standard library in "
"`Cargo.toml`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1101
msgid ""
"What syntax should be used for the explicit standard library dependencies? "
"`builtin = true`? `sysroot = true` (not ideal, as \"sysroot\" isn't a "
"concept that we typically introduce to end-users)?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1107
msgid "What is the format for builtin dependencies in `Cargo.lock`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1110
msgid ""
"How should `builtin` deps be represented in lockfiles? Is `builtin = true` "
"appropriate? Could the `source` field be reused with the string \"builtin\" "
"or should it stay only as a URL+scheme?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1116
msgid ""
"What syntax is used to patch dependencies on the standard library in `Cargo."
"toml`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1119
msgid ""
"`[patch.builtin]` is the natural syntax given `builtin` is a new source, but "
"may be needlessly different to existing packages. This mechanism exists only "
"for internal purposes so the exact syntax isn't especially important."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1125
msgid "Should implicit standard library dependencies default to public?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1128
msgid ""
"Implicit standard library dependencies defaulting to public is a trade-off "
"between special-casing in Cargo and requiring that any user with a "
"dependency on the standard library who re-exports from the standard library "
"manually declare their dependency as public."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1135
msgid "Should explicit standard library dependencies default to private?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1138
msgid ""
"Explicit standard library dependencies defaulting to private is a trade-off "
"between consistency with other dependencies in the manifest and implicit "
"standard library dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1144
msgid "Should we support `build-dependencies`?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1147
msgid ""
"Allowing `builtin` dependencies to be used in `dependencies` and `dev-"
"dependencies` but not in `build-dependencies` is an inconsistency."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1150
msgid ""
"However, supporting `builtin` dependencies in `build-dependencies` would "
"permit no-std build scripts. It is unclear whether supporting no-std build "
"scripts would be desirable. Not supporting `build-dependencies` initially is "
"a safe default that can be changed later if this is deemed necessary, "
"without breaking any existing users."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1156
msgid ""
"↩ [_`dev-dependencies` and `build-dependencies`_](#dev-dependencies-and-"
"build-dependencies)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1158
msgid "Should parsed manifests be used instead of the registry index?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1161
msgid ""
"An alternative to changing the registry index would be checking the parsed "
"manifests of dependencies - which are downloaded and available when the unit "
"graph is being built (and used for other Cargo features)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1167
msgid "Should `cargo metadata` include the standard library's dependencies?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1170
msgid ""
"`cargo metadata` is used by tools like rust-analyzer to determine the entire "
"crate graph and would benefit from knowledge of the standard library's "
"dependencies, but this leaks internal details of the standard library and is "
"counter to the intent behind opaque dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1175
msgid ""
"This is primarily a compatibility concern, though were `builtin` "
"dependencies to be included in the metadata, it is expected that it would "
"not be too disruptive, as:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1179
msgid ""
"`cargo pkgid` and `cargo build --message-format` will unconditionally use "
"the new `pkgid` spec anyway;"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1181
msgid ""
"[`cargo_metadata`](https://crates.io/crates/cargo_metadata) does not "
"currently parse the pkgid spec so this won't break all users;"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1183
msgid ""
"and this will also show up in the source which is still opaque and "
"`cargo_metadata` does not parse"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1186
msgid ""
"Therefore this would only be a problem for users who are parsing the pkgid "
"specs using `cargo-util-schemas` or their own parser, which is unlikely to "
"be disruptive."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1190
#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1200
msgid "↩ [_Cargo subcommands_](#cargo-subcommands)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1194
msgid ""
"What should the exact format of the `pkgid` spec for builtin dependencies be?"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1197
msgid ""
"The format for builtin dependencies of `cargo pkgid` can be changed prior to "
"stabilisation and does not need to match what is proposed in this RFC "
"exactly."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1202
msgid "Prior art"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1205
msgid ""
"See the [_Background_](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3873-build-std-"
"context.html#background) and [_History_](https://rust-lang.github.io/"
"rfcs/3873-build-std-context.html#history) of the build-std context RFC."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1208
msgid "Future possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1211
msgid ""
"This RFC unblocks fixing [rust-lang/cargo#8798](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"cargo/issues/8798), enabling no-std crates from being prevented from having "
"std dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1214
msgid "There are also many possible follow-ups to this part of the RFC:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1218
msgid ""
"Replace `#![no_std]` as the source-of-truth for whether a crate depends on "
"`std`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1221
msgid ""
"Crates can currently use the crate attribute `#![no_std]` to indicate a lack "
"of dependency on `std`. `#![no_std]` serves two purposes - it stops the "
"compiler from adding `std` to the extern prelude and it prevents the user "
"from depending on anything from `std` accidentally."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1226
msgid ""
"rustc's default behaviour of loading `std` when not explicitly provided the "
"crate via an `--extern` flag must be preserved for backwards-compatibility "
"with existing direct invocations of rustc."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1230
msgid ""
"Ideally, `#![no_std]` would be removed entirely and the compiler would only "
"load `std` if it were used, but this isn't possible with the current "
"compiler implementation."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1234
msgid ""
"Therefore, an explicit flag or attribute is necessary to tell rustc whether "
"to load `std`. `-Zcrate-attr=no_std` could be replaced with a explicit "
"compiler flag `--no-std` (naming subject to bikeshed) that Cargo and other "
"drivers of rustc could use. `#![no_std]` could be removed over an edition "
"alongside addition of builtin dependencies to the Cargo manifest."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1240
msgid ""
"As removing `#![no_std]` could easily be left to a follow-up, and is a "
"change to a stable attribute in the surface language (which would require "
"language team approval), it isn't included in this proposal to keep scope "
"and the number of required approvals small."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1247
msgid ""
"Allow unstable crate names to be referenced behind cfgs without requiring "
"nightly"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1250
msgid ""
"It is possible to allow builtin dependencies on unstable crate names to "
"exist behind cfgs and for the crate to be compiled on a stable toolchain as "
"long as the cfgs are not active. This is a trade-off - it adds a large "
"constraint on when Cargo can validate the set of crate names, but would "
"enable users to avoid using nightly or doing MSRV bumps."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1258
msgid "Allow `builtin` source replacement"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1261
msgid ""
"This involves allowing the user to blanket-override the standard library "
"sources with a `[source.builtin]` section of the Cargo configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1264
msgid ""
"As [rationale-source-replacement](#why-disallow-source-replacement-on-"
"builtin-packages) details it is unclear if users need to do this or if it's "
"even something the Rust project wishes to support."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1269
msgid "Remove `rustc_dep_of_std`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1272
msgid ""
"With first-class explicit dependencies on the standard library, "
"`rustc_dep_of_std` is rendered unnecessary and explicit dependencies on the "
"standard library can always be present in the `Cargo.toml` of the standard "
"library's dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1277
msgid ""
"The `core`, `alloc` and `std` dependencies can be patched in the standard "
"library's workspace to point to the local copy of the crates. This avoids "
"`crates.io` dependencies needing to add support for `rustc_dep_of_std` "
"before the standard library can depend on them."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1284
msgid "Allow enabling/disabling features with build-std"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1287
msgid ""
"This would require the library team be comfortable with the features "
"declared on the standard library being part of the stable interface of the "
"standard library."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1290
msgid ""
"The behaviour of disabling default features has been highlighted as a "
"potential cause of breaking changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1293
msgid ""
"Alternatively, this could be enabled alongside another proposal which would "
"allow the standard library to define some features as stable and others as "
"unstable."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1297
msgid ""
"As there are some features that Cargo will set itself when appropriate (e.g. "
"to enable or disable [panic runtimes](https://github.com/davidtwco/rfcs/blob/"
"build-std-part-two-always/text/3874-build-std-always.md#panic-strategies) or "
"[`compiler-builtins/mem`](https://github.com/davidtwco/rfcs/blob/build-std-"
"part-two-always/text/3874-build-std-always.md#compiler-builtinsmem)), Cargo "
"may need to always prevent some otherwise stable features from being toggled "
"as it controls those."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1307
msgid "Allow local builds of `compiler-rt` intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1310
msgid ""
"The [`c` feature](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3873-build-std-context."
"html#dependencies) of `compiler_builtins` (which is also exposed by `core`, "
"`alloc` and `std` through `compiler-builtins-c`) causes its `build.rs` file "
"to build and link in more optimised C versions of intrinsics."
msgstr ""

#: src/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.md:1314
msgid ""
"It will not be enabled by default because it is possible that the target "
"platform does not have a suitable C compiler available. The user being able "
"to enable this manually will be enabled through work on features (see "
"[_Allow enabling/disabling features with build-std_](#allow-"
"enablingdisabling-features-with-build-std)). Once the user can enable "
"`compiler-builtins/c`, they will need to manually configure `CFLAGS` to "
"ensure that the C components will link with Rust code."
msgstr ""
